<title>CANADA: British Columbia says to revise gas royalty system.</title>
<headline>British Columbia says to revise gas royalty system.</headline>
<dateline>VANCOUVER 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Columbia on Thursday asked the natural gas industry to contribute to a review of royalty price calculations.</p>
<p>The province said the aim of the review was to streamline the process and reduce inequities.</p>
<p>&quot;The growth of the natural gas industry in British Columbia and changes in the marketplace have made our royalty collection process increasingly complex and unnecessarily tedious,&quot; said Dan Miller, provincial minister of employment and investment.</p>
<p>&quot;We're looking at reducing whatever red tape we can and eliminating inequities that have developed.&quot;</p>
<p>The government will meet with royalty payers in Calgary on June 9 to discuss ideas.</p>
<p>((Reuters Vancouver Bureau (604) 664-7314))</p>
